Local adaptations consume the original striped K128/N64 weight payloads,
select BFP16-backed or native BF16 matrix multiplication with FP32 K-group
partials, preserve BF16 activation/output contracts, and execute the eight-column FFN
with fused SiLU/multiply. Adjacent N32 halves share one input/weight object
and dequantization scratch. Zero metadata uses exact BF16 bit construction.
